# WISE² Core project rules

Use `CLAUDE.md` as the shared WISE² architecture and product context. References there to Claude mean the active coding agent, including Cursor.

@CLAUDE.md

- This is a large, active pnpm/Turborepo monorepo. Inspect the nearest component `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or `CLAUDE.md` before changing it.
- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes. Never discard, overwrite, or broadly reformat user work outside the requested scope.
- Never read, print, commit, or copy secret values from `.env*`, credentials, certificates, or production configuration. Use tracked example files for variable names only.
- Use `pnpm` from the repository root and prefer workspace-scoped commands before full-repository commands.
- Before editing, inspect relevant code and git status. After editing, run the narrowest relevant type-check, lint, or test and state what was not verified.
- Ask before deployments, destructive commands, production data changes, external messages, purchases, or account-level configuration changes.
- Do not automatically create daily logs, decisions, reflections, or other operational records unless the user asks or the task materially requires one.

